PHASE 5: DATA SIMULATION (REALISTIC, NOT RANDOM)
Research Basis (Physiological Accuracy)
Medical device UIs must simulate realistic data patterns, not random noise. This teaches the frontend to handle real-world behavior.

Sources:

Cardiac physiology: systolic 120 mmHg, diastolic 80 mmHg (pulsatile)

Body temperature: baseline 37.2°C, natural variation ±0.5°C

Cardiac output: 4-6 L/min at rest

Heart rate: 60-100 bpm (variable RPM for pump)

Implementation Pattern
javascript
class RealisticSimulator {
  constructor() {
    this.baseTemp = 37.0;
    this.basePressure = 120;
    this.basePressureDiastolic = 80;
    this.baseFlow = 4.5;
    this.pumpRPM = 0; // User-controlled
    this.startTime = Date.now();
  }

  // TEMPERATURE: Gradual drift with micro-variations
  getTemperature() {
    const elapsed = (Date.now() - this.startTime) / 1000;
    const drift = Math.sin(elapsed / 60) * 0.3; // Slow drift
    const variation = Math.random() * 0.1 - 0.05; // Micro-variation
    return this.baseTemp + drift + variation;
  }

  // PRESSURE: Pulsatile curve (systolic/diastolic)
  getPressure() {
    const beat = (Date.now() % 1000) / 1000; // 1-second beat cycle
    const pulsatile = Math.sin(beat * Math.PI * 2);
    const systolic = this.basePressure + (pulsatile * 40);
    return Math.round(systolic);
  }

  // FLOW RATE: Correlated with pump RPM
  getFlowRate() {
    const correlation = (this.pumpRPM / 3000) * 2; // RPM affects flow
    const baseFlow = 4.5 + correlation;
    const variation = Math.random() * 0.5 - 0.25;
    return Math.max(0, Math.min(6, baseFlow + variation));
  }

  // PUMP RPM: Ramps smoothly, doesn't jump
  setPumpRPM(targetRPM) {
    const current = this.pumpRPM;
    const delta = Math.min(100, Math.abs(targetRPM - current));
    this.pumpRPM += (targetRPM > current) ? delta : -delta;
    return this.pumpRPM;
  }
}

// Usage:
const sim = new RealisticSimulator();
setInterval(() => {
  const data = {
    timestamp: new Date().toLocaleTimeString(),
    temperature: sim.getTemperature().toFixed(1),
    pressure: sim.getPressure(),
    flow: sim.getFlowRate().toFixed(2),
    rpm: Math.round(sim.pumpRPM)
  };
  updateDashboard(data);
}, 1000);
Why This Matters:

Real-world pressure is pulsatile (varies with heartbeat)

Real-world temperature drifts slowly (not random jumps)

Flow correlates with pump speed (realistic physics)

UI learns to handle patterns, not chaos

